<title>Hydronephrosis: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0644-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Hydronephrosis on prenatal ultrasound. Order ultrasound postnatally at 1 week and 1 month. Both results normal?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-2">
<label>No further workup necessary.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Order VCUG. Vesicoureteral reflux?</label>
<path target="cell-4">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Dimercaptosuccinic acid scan.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>APPD &lt;10 mm (on postnatal ultrasound)?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Serial ultrasounds.</label>
<path target="cell-7">If not resolving</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Order diuretic renography. Consistent with decreased or worsening renal function and&#x002F;or obstruction?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Consider pyeloplasty.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
